# Git Commit Conventions

## Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

[optional body]
```

- **Subject line** (first line): `type(scope): subject` — total ≤ 72 characters
- **Blank line** between subject and body (when body is present)
- **Body lines**: each line wraps at 72 characters; explains *why*, not *what*

## Types

| Type | When to use |
|---|---|
| `feat` | New feature or user-facing behaviour |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `refactor` | Code change that neither adds a feature nor fixes a bug |
| `test` | Adding or updating tests |
| `docs` | Documentation or spec changes only |
| `chore` | Tooling, deps, build scripts, config (no production code) |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `db` | Schema migration or database-level change |

## Scopes

Use the feature module name or a cross-cutting label:

**Cross-cutting:** `infra` · `arch` · `config` · `ci` · `shared`

**Feature modules** (add as they land): `auth` · `vehicles` · `owners` · `leads` · `inventory` · `sales`

Omit scope only when the change is truly global (e.g. `chore: upgrade pnpm to 11.x`).

## Subject Rules

- Imperative mood — "add", "fix", "remove", not "added", "fixed", "removed"
- No period at the end
- No capitalisation of first word after the colon (unless a proper noun)
- Describe the effect, not the mechanism: "add vehicle listing guard" not "add if-check to use case"

## Examples

```
# ✅ Good
feat(vehicles): add vehicle listing status guard
fix(leads): prevent duplicate lead assignment
refactor(infra): extract VehicleVin into value object
test(shared): add unit tests for CalendarDate
docs(arch): add ADR-0001 for logical CQRS
db(vehicles): add index on status and created_at
chore: upgrade pnpm to 11.10.0

# ❌ Bad
Fixed the bug                          ← no type/scope, past tense, vague
feat: Added vehicle listing guard.     ← past tense, trailing period
WIP                                    ← not a valid commit to push
```
